package Protocol::7::Coding::Helper::EnforceQuota;

use strict;
use warnings;

use Protocol::7::Config;
use Protocol::7::Log qw(log_warn);

sub enforce_quota {
    my ($job, $usage) = @_;

    my $quota = Protocol::7::Config->get(
        'coding.helper.enforce_quota.quota',
        { default => 4096 },
    );

    if ($usage > $quota) {
        log_warn(
            'Job %s byte usage (%d) exceeded quota (%d)',
            $job->id,
            $usage,
            $quota,
        );
        return 0;  # FALSE
    }

    return 1;  # TRUE
}

1;
```

**Time complexity:** O(1) — single config lookup and comparison.
**Space complexity:** O(1) — no additional data structures.

**Notes:**
- Quota is read per-call from config; for high-frequency calls, consider caching the value in a package-level variable.
- The function returns `0` (FALSE) on quota exceedance, `1` (TRUE) on success.
- Logging includes job ID and numeric values for auditability.
